From: Olekhov Vasilii <olekhov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: usb: qmi_wwan: add Quectel EM060K-GL (2c7c:030b)

The Quectel EM060K-GL requires the host to assert DTR on USB interface 4
(via SET_CONTROL_LINE_STATE class request) before its QMI service becomes
responsive. Without QMI_WWAN_QUIRK_DTR the driver binds successfully —
cdc-wdm0 and wwan0 are created, raw_ip=Y — but all uqmi requests time out.

Present in GL.iNET GL-E750v2 (M.2 B-key slot, connected via USB).

Signed-off-by: Olekhov Vasilii <olekhov@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/usb/qmi_wwan.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/net/usb/qmi_wwan.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/qmi_wwan.c
@@ -1086,4 +1086,5 @@
    {QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x0125)},	/* Quectel EC25, EC20 R2.0  Mini PCIe */
    {QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x0306)},	/* Quectel EP06/EG06/EM06 */
+	{QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x030b)},   /* Quectel EM060K-GL */
    {QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x0512)},	/* Quectel EG12/EM12 */
    {QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x0620)},	/* Quectel EM160R-GL */